
/*

Name: Uzma Ejaz

Date:11/07/2026

Description: Aggregate Functions |  What are our all-time global sales?



The  Music Company Formatted Staff Contact List



The office manager needs a clean staff contact list for the internal company directory. She needs each employee's name in a consistent format: last name in uppercase followed by a comma and their first name; alongside their standardized lowercase email address and job title.



Your job is to use SQL string functions to produce this formatted list for the Music internal company directory.


Output should contain 3 columns and 8 rows:

 StaffName - last name in UPPERCASE, comma, then first name (e.g., ADAMS, Andrew)

 EmailAddress - email address in all lowercase

 Title - the employee's job title

Requirements:

- Select from the Employee table

- Use UPPER on LastName

- Use || to concatenate the name: UPPER(LastName) || ', ' || FirstName

- Use LOWER on Email

- Sort results alphabetically by LastName

- Include a comment stating the purpose of the query

*/

SELECT

UPPER(LastName) || ',' || FirstName AS StaffName,

 LOWER(Email) AS EmailAddress,

 Title

FROM 

Employee

ORDER BY 

LastName 


